@champtar Hi, sorry took me a moment to find time to look at this. Since I worked on the PCI NIC naming scheme changes for s390 I guess I'm indeed the right person to ask. That said I'm a little confused. We don't have ACPI on s390 and probably won't ever get it either. So I'm especially wondering about the same question @poettering asked, if there is no `firmware_node/sun` file then I too would expect a fallback to the existing handling which works for s390. From the code I'd be afraid that distributions might turn on the new naming scheme and then we would need that fallback, no?

Maybe some additional background. On s390 Linux which always executes under at least a machine hypersivor PCI hotplug slots aren't really physical slots, rather the hypervisor does per-PCI-function pass-through and the hotplug slot name number is a hypervisor provided identifier for that PCI function. And we did add special handling for this as the
hotplug slot name is a hexadecimal number which used to cause issues. This is why we have s390 specific handling as explained [in this comment](https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/83c298547230039782c7ddc29446925dd268dfe4/src/udev/udev-builtin-net_id.c#L417).
